\title{SAT\_O4 Audit Instructions}
\date{2025-06-03}

\begin{document}

\maketitle

\section*{Abstract}
This document defines the audit instructions for Module O4, covering the Cosmological Constant Derivation in the SAT\_O emergent filament framework.

\section*{Scope}
Audit of the SAT\_O4 Module: Cosmological Constant Derivation.

\section*{Methods}
Audit threads must rigorously follow the SAT\_O Testing Protocol (Ultra-Hostile Upgrade). Each audit must address the following:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{Definition Consistency}
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Confirm all terms used match the SAT\_O Glossary (v1).
        \item Particular focus on: \( G_{\text{induced}} \), \( \Lambda_{\text{induced}} \), \( \ell_f \), filament tension \( T \), rigidity \( A \).
    \end{itemize}

    \item \textbf{Logical Structure Validation}
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Validate logical consistency of emergent derivations.
        \item Specific focus: derivation of \( G_{\text{induced}} \) and \( \Lambda_{\text{induced}} \) from filament parameters.
    \end{itemize}

    \item \textbf{Mathematical Correctness}
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Check dimensional correctness of \( G_{\text{induced}} \) and \( \Lambda_{\text{induced}} \).
        \item Validate the formula \( \ell_f = (2A/T)^{1/3} \) and its usage.
        \item Confirm proper handling of logarithmic expressions.
    \end{itemize}

    \item \textbf{Falsifiability Assessment}
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Explicitly demonstrate a falsifiability condition for \( \Lambda_{\text{induced}} \).
        \item Describe how \( \ell_f \) could be empirically falsified.
    \end{itemize}

    \item \textbf{Independence Verification}
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Confirm derivations rely only on definitions within SAT\_O4 and SAT\_O Glossary.
    \end{itemize}

    \item \textbf{Hidden Parameter Scan}
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Identify hidden assumptions about filament distributions or densities.
        \item Confirm no arbitrary free parameters inserted.
    \end{itemize}

    \item \textbf{Failure Mode Analysis}
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Formulate at least one plausible failure mode for \( \Lambda_{\text{induced}} \) derivation.
    \end{itemize}

    \item \textbf{Quantum Consistency Check}
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Verify that filament structure implies quantum stability consistent with effective \( \hbar_{\text{eff}} \) derivation.
    \end{itemize}
\end{enumerate}

\section*{Deliverables}
Each audit thread must submit:

\begin{itemize}
    \item A full \LaTeX\ audit report including:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Abstract
        \item Scope (SAT\_O4)
        \item Methods
        \item Findings
        \item Critical Commentary
    \end{itemize}
    \item An audit checklist covering all categories above.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Note}: No pass/fail criteria or solution hints should be included in the audit report.

\end{document}
```

